# NOTE on max-line-length (configured at 170, not the usual 120):
# The EIP-712 typehash preimages in AgentIdentity.sol, MemoryLedger.sol and
# MemoryAccessControl.sol are single string literals that must NOT be wrapped.
# Solidity concatenates adjacent literals so the hash would be unaffected, but
# splitting them breaks the backend conformance tests that scan these .sol files
# to prove src/protocol/eip712.js matches the on-chain definitions, and makes the
# preimage un-greppable. solhint ignores inline disables for this rule, so the
# limit is raised globally instead. Nothing else in the tree exceeds 120.
